cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software-code
title: "IntELiMon Decision Support Tool"
abstract: >-
   The IntELiMon Decision Support Tool is an open-source Shiny dashboard that returns results from the
   Interagency Ecosystem Lidar Monitoring Program in a format that supports planning and evaluation of
   treatment success. In the program, managers collect Terrestrial Laser Scans (TLS) which record the
   three-dimensional structure of vegetation and fuel at monitoring plots. These TLS scans are then submitted
   to a national dataset at USGS EROS where the complex structural data is summarized as standard forestry,
   fuels, and ecology metrics along with custom models developed and calibrated for
   individual sites. The tool serves these metrics back to managers, grouping selected plots around user-
   defined treatment dates and presenting their change over time. Additional features are provided to estimate
   potential changes in fire behavior from changes to canopy structure over time under a single weather
   scenario, experimental features that generate inputs for future use in other standard fire and forestry
   tools, and a feature that assembles figures and tables from the user's analysis into an editable report.
   The tool is hosted as a web-app which provides access to publicly available data, and when run from a
   desktop R console, allows private data to be analyzed alongside the publicly available dataset. This
   release is a beta version; several features are still under development.
